WEBVTT

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:58.290
Spring's here.

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:06.600
Excuse me.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.160
Take your time.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.440
What's wrong?

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.460
Is there something
stuck on my face?

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.190
Not at all.

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:33.530
Really?

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.030
Godai?

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:43.030
Yeah?

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.740
Do you own
a necktie?

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:06.500
This way?

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.560
Dammit!

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:12.160
Umm--

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.470
Maybe this'll do.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:23.410
Once I start doing office work,
this'll be an everyday struggle.

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:27.520
Then again--

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.220
Kyoko,
I'm off to work!

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.780
Darling! Darling!

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:39.560
You can't go out to the office
with your tie looking like this!

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:43.330
A neat appearance is
one factor in promotions.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:47.840
You make me do
this everyday!

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.460
You're just like a child!

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:52.380
Kyoko--

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:58.520
No honey! Not so early
in the morning!

00:03:58.720 --> 00:03:59.690
Kyoko!

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:09.750
That hurt!

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.100
What!?

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:17.130
Going out?

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:18.930
What is it?

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:22.800
Something strange is
developing over there.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.800
In the manager's room?

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.910
Yeah, something's up.

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:33.750
I'm so glad to see
you in good health.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:36.550
Yes, my back seems fine.
Thank you.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.380
Mr. Otonashi--

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.980
Yeah, meetin' with
the manager's folks.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.410
Kyoko, we'll be
waiting outside.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:45.590
Okay!

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:47.850
Up we go.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:48.900
Mr. Otonashi.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.690
You're too kind.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:52.390
Well, shall we be off?

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:58.430
All that nice-nice talk
is really suspicious.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:01.840
Something's up for sure!

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.540
Yeah, isn't today--

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:16.520
Manager?

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:19.660
Hello.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:21.660
Headin' out somewhere?

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:24.860
You're visiting
Soichiro's grave?

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:25.830
Yes.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:31.510
That explains why
the folks were all here.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.870
It's more than that.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:39.580
Last year they made up some excuse
and didn't come.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:41.840
I see.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:47.660
I'll be back by evening.
Keep an eye on things.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:48.440
Roger.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:49.840
I uh--

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:53.420
N-Nothing.
Hurry home.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:55.430
Okay. I will.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:06.560
She's not going to fight with
her parents at the cemetery?

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:19.940
Mr. Otonashi is so nice
they'll trap him in their plan for sure!

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:23.380
Damn! I should never
have made that date!

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:31.460
But I'd never have been
invited to the gravesite, anyway.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:34.330
Boo!

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:39.000
Kozue!?

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:41.470
Did I scare you?

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:42.870
Yeah!

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:53.090
The tie looks great!

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:55.260
You told me to wear it.

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:02.630
Let's go!

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:03.890
Go? Go where?

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:05.630
Shopping. Come help.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:09.300
Shopping? You made me wear
a tie to go shopping?

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:10.490
Come on!

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:19.640
A melon?

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:21.490
And a necktie?

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:23.880
What's the connection?

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:30.240
Kozue? What're we
buying a melon for?

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:31.960
Come with me
and find out.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.140
A housing tract?

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:51.480
Not too bad.
He'll do me proud.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:55.110
Right here.

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:00.480
Thi-- Thi--
Thi-- Thi--

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:01.850
It's my place!

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:03.480
Here.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:10.330
Welcome!

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:12.300
H-Hold it, Kozue!

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:14.300
You never said a word--

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:18.270
Come on, Godai.
Don't be shy.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:19.940
H-Hey!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:23.240
I'm not ready--
It's so sudden--

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:24.640
Hey!

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:39.790
I-I'm Yusaku Godai.
S-Sorry to barge in on you!

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.630
He seems sincere enough.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:43.860
Relieved, Daddy?

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:45.600
Okay, here we go.

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:49.160
How kind of you to
bring such a nice gift.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:51.330
Godai brought
the perfect gift!

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:55.100
Oh, no! I'm caught
in Kozue's plot!

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.170
Did you kiss
him already?

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:00.740
Well?
Did you?

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:01.980
It's a secret.

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:03.690
You KNOW we haven't!

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.450
'Fess up!
How far've you gone?

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:07.360
Yosuke!

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:08.890
We haven't gone
anywhere--

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:10.740
You can't lie to me!

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:12.130
Yosuke!

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:17.520
Be nice! This guy could
soon be your big brother!

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:20.630
I didn't do nothin'!
Ow! That hurts!

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:24.570
W-What have I gotten myself into?
We haven't even kissed yet!

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:26.030
Mister Godai!

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:29.610
Be sure to treat
my daughter right.

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:33.310
Kozue is still
our little girl!

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:34.970
Yes, sir!

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:54.600
Come on in.

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:07.730
I'm sure Soichiro appreciated
your gift of incense.

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:13.470
If my husband wasn't ill,
we'd have been here last year, too.

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:15.580
It couldn't be helped.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:24.220
Soichiro--

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:30.330
Forgive me for not coming more
often. I'll bet you've been lonely.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:37.070
Please don't wory about me.
I love my life at Maison Ikkoku.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:40.990
Time certainly flies.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.010
It's been two years
since Soichiro passed on.

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:48.540
A full two years.

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:50.580
Yes. Two years.

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:57.720
Despite two long years, I'm
sure you haven't forgotten him.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.240
No.

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:03.990
But I'm more concerned
about Kyoko at this point.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:12.640
She should not grieve
like this forever.

00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:19.480
Father!

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:22.640
I've given this
a great deal of thought.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:27.720
You can't go on
like this forever.

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:31.890
You're so young.

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:35.790
You should come out from
the shelter of the Otonashi home.

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:37.460
Father, you don't mean--

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:45.810
Did you recruit
Mr. Otonashi?

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:47.330
Not yet.

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:51.180
Why-- Why would
you say that!?

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:57.910
I should just start over? Are you
saying I should forget Soichiro!?

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:04.450
Father!

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:12.140
Kyoko.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:13.240
Yes?

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:14.990
In olden times...

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:20.510
...they'd write the widow's name
on the tombstone when a man died.

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:23.470
The word for widow.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:27.410
In Japanese it means
one who has yet to die.

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:30.510
"One who has yet to die."

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:34.320
But that's wrong!

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:39.990
You don't have "yet to die."
You're still alive!

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:24.430
He put it perfectly, Ritsuko.

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:26.540
Just what I wanted to say.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:32.780
Kyoko, you must put
Soichiro behind you.

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:42.310
I've become a burden to
the Otonashi family, is that it?

00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:47.990
D-Don't be ridiculous.
You've been a great blessing!

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:52.320
I'm happy that you still
care so much for him.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.940
But your own life--

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:59.630
Then please allow me to
impose on you a little longer.

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:00.630
Kyoko!

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:03.510
Don't you understand what
your father-in-law is saying?

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:05.580
Yes, I do.

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:11.450
I know in my heart that
what he says is reasonable.

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:13.220
Still,  I-

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:16.760
Kyoko, what do
you intend to do?

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:18.240
I don't know.

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:22.230
But until I know
my future path...

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:25.630
...I'd like to keep
Soichiro's name.

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:31.300
Nice words!

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:34.640
But what happens when
you're old and lonely!?

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:37.480
You still cannot find
someone else to love?

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:39.410
Well, Kyoko?

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:44.410
What is wrong with you!?
We're here before Soichiro's grave!

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:45.480
Sorry.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:17.640
I'm so glad that
Mom and Dad like you!

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:24.640
Maybe, but meeting them so
formally, it's like--

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:26.390
Like what?

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:28.130
I mean--
You see--

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:30.660
Our parents have
to meet, right?

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:34.570
A wedding is between two
families, not just two people.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:38.800
Weddi ng!? When did we
jump to that conclusion!?

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:43.710
Engagements go more smoothly
once the parents meet.

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:45.880
That's true, huh?

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:48.170
Parents?

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:54.680
Can I get along with
parents like those?

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:02.930
--Can you get along with them?
--I'm doomed!

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:05.860
No! I was
thinking out loud.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:14.510
Kozue, don't you think
we're doing this out of order?

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:15.610
How so?

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:21.240
Doesn't this happen when the guy
and girl are a confirmed couple?

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:25.420
That's true. We haven't
taken the leap, have we?

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:28.160
So why haven't
you leaped?

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:42.390
~Ki'ss her?
~Ki'ss hernot?

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:44.040
It's just a kiss, right?

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:45.870
Hold on a sec!

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:51.010
Gotta eat when
the table's set!

00:17:57.190 --> 00:17:59.210
You've defiled my daughter!

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:03.850
Show your good intentions! Let's get
that marriage license now!

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.690
Kozue's still
our little girl!

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.820
C-Come on!

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:12.060
I-It was just a kiss!

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:14.000
"Just a kiss"?

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:19.540
Is that your attitude
when you deflower my daughter!?

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:24.910
M-Mother, please
say something!

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:30.540
"Mother?" Hear that Darling?
Godai just called me "Mother"!

00:18:31.390 --> 00:18:32.220
I--

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.910
Then you agree!?
Say it to me, too!

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.760
Go ahead and
call him "Dad"!

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:37.820
Well!?

00:18:37.890 --> 00:18:38.760
Well!?

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:39.810
WELL!?

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:01.790
Godai!

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:05.380
Now I can give my heart
to Mitaka with no regrets!

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:07.490
We're getting married!

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:12.460
N-No, Kyoko!
It's all a big mistake!

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:18.900
See ya!

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:30.500
Kyoko!

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:48.060
Hey, somebody's
at the window!

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:50.990
It's gotta be
my brother!

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:54.100
Nobody's there-

00:19:55.680 --> 00:19:57.970
I must've been
seeing things.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:19:59.880
That's weird.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.230
Godai, hurry up!

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:29.360
I'll be back by evening.

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:34.040
What's wrong, Godai?

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:38.770
I'll be back by evening.

00:20:47.190 --> 00:20:48.850
What is it, Godai?

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:53.390
Uhh--
Kozue--?

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:10.270
There's no way they'd let
her visit the grave in peace.

00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:14.150
I knew this would
depress her. I knew it!

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:18.920
Forgive me Kyoko! I didn't
mean to get side-tracked!

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:21.190
Why did I do this to you!?

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:26.090
If I was worried, why didn't
I fIy to your side? Kyoko!

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:42.930
I knew from the start
that I was useless!

00:21:48.020 --> 00:21:49.980
I'm useless, but--

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:55.250
I can only try to
cheer you up, but--

00:21:57.260 --> 00:21:58.280
But even so--

00:21:58.700 --> 00:22:02.190
You don't know anything! Not even
when Mr. Otonashi explains it!

00:22:02.470 --> 00:22:04.130
Prepare for your future!

00:22:04.610 --> 00:22:08.010
Be quiet! When will you get tired
of repeating the same thing!?

00:22:10.180 --> 00:22:13.110
You don't listen no matter
how many times we say it!

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:14.610
Stop following me!

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:17.110
Don't you understand what
we're trying to do?

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:19.370
Don't you have
anywhere else to be?

00:22:19.550 --> 00:22:21.780
You COULD use
your maiden name!

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:23.450
Go away!

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:25.080
'Scuse me--

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:27.850
When are you going to
grow out of this melodrama?

00:22:27.930 --> 00:22:30.890
Keep your voice down!
People are staring!

00:22:31.100 --> 00:22:34.260
They're staring because of
the awful things you're saying!

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:39.300
You're being awful! I'm an adult!
I can live as I like!

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:42.270
A child is always
a child to her parents!

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:43.890
I can speak my mind!

00:22:43.980 --> 00:22:45.200
"Speak" somewhere else!

00:22:45.410 --> 00:22:48.570
We're looking out
for your happiness!

00:22:48.650 --> 00:22:51.240
My happiness is
just fine, now!

00:22:51.320 --> 00:22:51.970
Excuse me--

00:22:52.050 --> 00:22:54.410
What's happy
about being a widow!?

00:22:54.490 --> 00:22:55.950
It's a difference of values!

00:22:56.020 --> 00:23:00.080
Stop being martyrs and
make yourselves happy!

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:00.990
Excuse me--

00:23:01.060 --> 00:23:04.620
I wanted a son! You could
give me a son-in-law!

00:23:04.800 --> 00:23:07.820
There's nothing wrong with
wanting a son-in-law!

00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:11.060
Then don't get married!
Just come home!

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:12.960
Shut up!

00:23:13.140 --> 00:23:15.830
Aren't you ashamed
acting like this?

00:23:16.340 --> 00:23:18.830
What child says "Shut up"
to her parents!

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:21.930
A child who's fed up!
Shut up!

00:23:22.020 --> 00:23:25.380
When you're this stubborn
I've got half a mind to--

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:28.410
Shut up! Shut up!
Shut up!

00:23:28.490 --> 00:23:30.210
Are you listening to me, Kyoko!?

00:23:30.290 --> 00:23:33.810
You won't manipulate me!
Shut up!

00:23:35.630 --> 00:23:39.760
A guy couldn't wedge
his way into that family.

00:23:41.440 --> 00:23:42.530
I give up.

00:23:50.480 --> 00:23:53.810
Playing barefoot in the waves.
Gulls soaring through the sky!

00:23:53.880 --> 00:23:56.400
The ocean in springtime
is still cold, but--

00:23:57.420 --> 00:24:01.610
Next: "In this Corneri.
Godai vs. Mitaka! Clash of Proposals"

00:24:02.090 --> 00:24:05.380
Someday we'll all
look back on this and--

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:07.180
Soichiro--
